Description: open directories read-only, not with O_PATH
 libarchive's extraction opens each directory of a path to look for symlinks
 (la_opendirat) with O_PATH where there is one. musl defines O_ACCMODE as
 03|O_PATH, and Jam OS's open (user/posix/sys/file.c, open_dir) tests
 `(flags & O_ACCMODE) != O_RDONLY`, so open(dir, O_PATH|O_DIRECTORY) fails
 with EISDIR: every extraction stopped at its first entry ("Could not open
 ..: Is a directory"). A plain read-only open of a directory is what
 libarchive does where O_PATH, O_SEARCH and O_EXEC are all missing. Remove
 this patch when the layer takes O_PATH on a directory.
Forwarded: not-needed (works around a Jam OS layer bug; upstream's code is right for Linux)
---
--- a/libarchive/archive_write_disk_posix.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_write_disk_posix.c
@@ -450,15 +450,7 @@
 #if defined(O_DIRECTORY)
 	    | O_DIRECTORY
 #endif
-#if defined(O_PATH)
-	    | O_PATH
-#elif defined(O_SEARCH)
-	    | O_SEARCH
-#elif defined(__FreeBSD__) && defined(O_EXEC)
-	    | O_EXEC
-#else
 	    | O_RDONLY
-#endif
 	    ;
 
 #if !defined(HAVE_OPENAT)
